From: Tab S6 mainline port
Subject: [PATCH] drm/simpledrm: offer native ARGB8888 on gts6lwifi

The firmware framebuffer on this board is ARGB8888, but the generic format
list helper advertises only XRGB8888. CPU samples during window movement
show drm_fb_xrgb8888_to_argb8888_line as a significant hotspot. Offer the
native ARGB format as well, retaining XRGB fallback support. KWin 6.7.5
prefers an alpha-capable format of otherwise equal precision.

Limit the additional format to this board and native ARGB8888. This does
not change the framebuffer's alpha interpretation, remove the CPU copy,
or add physical vblank synchronization. Tested on 6.12.0-t860-gpu1: KWin
selects AR24, colors and touch are normal, and the conversion hotspot is gone.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/simpledrm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/simpledrm.c
@@ -949,8 +949,21 @@
 
 	/* Primary plane */
 
-	nformats = drm_fb_build_fourcc_list(dev, &format->format, 1,
-					    sdev->formats, ARRAY_SIZE(sdev->formats));
+	/*
+	 * This board's firmware scanout uses ARGB8888. The generic helper
+	 * advertises its non-alpha counterpart, requiring an opaque-alpha
+	 * conversion on every update. Also offer the actual native format
+	 * so compositors can avoid that conversion. Keep the generic formats
+	 * as fallbacks and leave the hardware framebuffer format unchanged.
+	 */
+	nformats = 0;
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,gts6lwifi") &&
+	    format->format == DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888)
+		sdev->formats[nformats++] = format->format;
+
+	nformats += drm_fb_build_fourcc_list(dev, &format->format, 1,
+					     sdev->formats + nformats,
+					     ARRAY_SIZE(sdev->formats) - nformats);
 
 	primary_plane = &sdev->primary_plane;
 	ret = drm_universal_plane_init(dev, primary_plane, 0, &simpledrm_primary_plane_funcs,
